# dagron — what must never be committed, in this tree and in the public mirror.
#
# This file exists as much for the mirror as for here. `.ossync.yaml` publishes this directory
# to lucheeseng827/dagron, and until it listed a `.gitignore` the mirror shipped none at all —
# so the two files below were ignored in the monorepo (by the root `.gitignore`) and ignored
# nowhere in the repository the quickstart actually tells people to clone.

# `make backup` defaults DIR=. — the working tree. scripts/backup-postgres.sh states what a
# dump holds: "every secret's ciphertext and every user row". It sets `umask 077`, which stops
# another local user reading it and does nothing at all about `git add -A`.
*.dump

# The session jar `make login` writes, and `make api-submit` reads. The monorepo's root
# `.gitignore` catches it under a blanket `*.txt`; the mirror inherits no such rule.
cookies.txt

# Written by `make edge-config` between `printf` and `dagron config`, and removed by its trap.
# Listed so an interrupted run does not leave an untracked file that looks like configuration.
.dagron-edge.yaml

# Generated by the Pi load rig (loadtest/pi/run.sh) — CSV samples and fleet logs, per run.
loadtest/pi/results/

# A SQLite database, its WAL and its shared-memory file, created when a `--db`
# flag lands where a path was expected and sqlite opens the flag itself as the
# filename. Three of these were committed by accident (86bfcde) and carried
# 1.4 MB of a scratch engine database into the tree. Ignored so the next
# mis-parse leaves an untracked file rather than a commit.
--db
--db-shm
--db-wal
